    <edge id="e1622" source="mlsys.recovery-objectives" target="mlsys.checkpoint-interval"><data key="relation">limits</data><data key="statement">caps the longest acceptable</data><data key="conditions">When recovery restarts from the last checkpoint and the RPO is shorter than the interval that failure rate and write cost would otherwise favor.</data></edge>
    <edge id="e1623" source="mlsys.recovery-objectives" target="mlsys.replication-failover"><data key="relation">determines</data><data key="statement">sets the recovery speed required of</data><data key="conditions">When the RTO is shorter than the time to restore from a checkpoint, so a standby must take over.</data></edge>
    <edge id="e1624" source="mlsys.incremental-checkpointing" target="mlsys.checkpoint"><data key="relation">implements</data><data key="statement">produces, as a base plus a chain of changes,</data><data key="conditions">When only a fraction of the state, such as touched embedding rows, changes between checkpoints.</data></edge>
